# Web endpoints

Standard skeleton:

```php
<?php
declare(strict_types=1);
require_once __DIR__ . '/notam_lib.php';

try {
    $pdo = notam_get_db_connection();
    notam_ensure_schema($pdo);
    notam_require_geojson_format();
    // ... endpoint logic ...
    header('Content-Type: application/json');
    echo json_encode($response);
} catch (InvalidArgumentException $e) {
    notam_send_error_response(400, $e);
} catch (RuntimeException $e) {
    notam_send_error_response(503, $e);
} catch (Throwable $e) {
    notam_send_error_response(500, $e);
}
```

## Rules

- `notam.php` and `status.php` MUST be DB-only. Do not import or call any FAA HTTP helper here.
- FAA-touching endpoints (`notam_live.php`, `notam_compare.php`, `faa_connectivity_test.php`) MUST guard with both:
  1. an enable env flag (e.g. `NOTAM_ALLOW_LIVE_PROXY`), and
  2. `notam_require_optional_shared_secret('NOTAM_LIVE_PROXY_KEY')` (or `FAA_CONNECTIVITY_KEY`).
  In production with no secret configured, the endpoint must stay disabled.
- Set `Content-Type: application/json` before writing the body.
- When serving cached data, also emit relevant `X-NOTAM-*` headers (`X-NOTAM-Source`, `X-NOTAM-Last-Delta-Sync`, `X-NOTAM-Last-Full-Reconcile`, `X-NOTAM-Sync-Age-Seconds`, optionally `X-NOTAM-Maintenance`).
- Validate query params via `notam_parse_query_parameters()`. Don't read `$_GET` directly for lat/lon/radius.
- Parse delta requests via `notam_parse_delta_request()`. Don't re-implement JSON body parsing.
- Never call `exit` directly inside `try`; let `notam_send_error_response` do it on errors.
